The fix is to ensure `json_dumps` can be called with just the item as the first positional argument.

```python
def json_convertor_default(default_mapping):
    def convertor(obj):
        if default_mapping and type(obj) in default_mapping:
            return default_mapping[type(obj)](obj)
        if type(obj) in JSON_CONVERTOR:
            return JSON_CONVERTOR[type(obj)](obj)
        raise TypeError(f'We do not know how to convert {obj} of type {type(obj)} for json serialization. Please pass the default_mapping parameter with proper mapping of the object to a basic python type.')
    return convertor
```

